  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For the reaction given below:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>xNH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo></math></p><p>If two equivalents of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgCl</mi></math> precipitate out, then the&nbsp;value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> will be _______</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi>xNH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><munder><mrow><mi>AgCl</mi><mo>&#8595;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow></munder></math></p><p>For 2 moles of AgCl precipitate out,only two chloride ions should be present out side the coordination sphere that is&nbsp;in the ionization sphere.</p><p>Hence, the formula of the complex should be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><munder><mrow><mi>AgCl</mi><mo>&#8595;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow></munder></math></p><p>So, the value of x should be 5.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
}